│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially weighted moving average with a causal adaptive                  │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman filter. Unlike a window average, the state explicitly models     │
│                          │ both level and local slope, allowing it to follow genuine directional motion with         │
│                          │ substantially less phase lag. The measurement-noise estimate is updated from clipped      │
│                          │ innovations, preventing transient outliers from causing spurious slope reversals. Process │
│                          │ uncertainty is adapted from persistent innovation magnitude so the filter becomes         │
│                          │ responsive during real regime changes while remaining smooth in quiet periods.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned samples remain aligned with the last sample of each original sliding window  │
│                          │ (`window_size - 1:`), preserving the existing public output-length contract and           │
│                          │ downstream alignment logic. The filter is O(N), has constant memory, and avoids expensive │
│                          │ multi-scale transforms or non-causal processing.                                          │
