│ patch_description        │ Add a confidence-gated hysteresis mechanism to the Kalman slope update. The level         │
│                          │ measurement update remains fully responsive, preserving low lag and tracking accuracy.    │
│                          │ However, a proposed slope reversal is only accepted after it is supported by consecutive, │
│                          │ sufficiently strong slope estimates. This prevents a single noisy innovation from         │
│                          │ flipping the estimated trend direction, directly reducing slope changes and false         │
│                          │ reversals.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The threshold is scaled from the adaptive innovation variance and inversely related to    │
│                          │ the sliding-window duration, so it adapts to signal volatility rather than using a fixed  │
│                          │ amplitude threshold. Small slope estimates are softly damped near zero, further           │
│                          │ suppressing jitter without blocking genuine sustained trend changes.                      │
