│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_trend                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed exponentially weighted moving average with a causal adaptive            │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman trend filter. The filter estimates both level and slope, so its  │
│                          │ prediction step compensates for much of the delay normally introduced by smoothing.       │
│                          │ Measurement uncertainty is estimated robustly from the recent innovation history using    │
│                          │ MAD, allowing the gain to decrease during noisy intervals and increase when the signal    │
│                          │ makes a sustained move. Innovation clipping limits the effect of isolated spikes,         │
│                          │ reducing noise-induced directional reversals without clipping legitimate broader trend    │
│                          │ changes.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned samples remain aligned with the end of each sliding window, preserving the   │
│                          │ existing output length and downstream delay assumptions. Computational cost is O(N) with  │
│                          │ constant-size state updates after initialization.                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
