│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the high tracking accuracy and low lag of the adaptive            │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman design with the lower false-reversal behavior of exponentially   │
│                          │ weighted sliding-window smoothing.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The enhanced path uses a robust adaptive Kalman level/slope estimator as the primary      │
│                          │ real-time tracker. Its output is then passed through a lightweight trend-aware consensus  │
│                          │ stage: an exponentially weighted window estimate provides stable local context, while a   │
│                          │ predictive alpha-beta correction preserves current trend direction and avoids ordinary    │
│                          │ moving-average delay. The blend is adaptive: when the Kalman estimate and local trend     │
│                          │ estimate agree, smoothing is increased to suppress noise-induced reversals; when they     │
│                          │ diverge during a genuine transition, the Kalman estimate dominates to retain              │
│                          │ responsiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The basic mode retains its original behavior and output shape, but uses a cumulative-sum  │
│                          │ implementation for efficient O(n) moving averages.                                        │
