╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ robust_trend_kalman                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially weighted moving average with a causal robust local-linear       │
│                          │ estimator followed by a lightweight alpha-beta trend tracker with reversal hysteresis.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The local-linear fit predicts at the newest sample in each window, removing the inherent  │
│                          │ trailing-average delay while retaining sliding-window noise suppression. Median/MAD       │
│                          │ clipping limits the influence of impulsive samples and non-stationary outliers. The       │
│                          │ adaptive tracker uses local slope evidence to increase gain during genuine directional    │
│                          │ motion and lower gain during noise-dominated flat periods. Finally, a noise-scaled        │
│                          │ hysteresis band suppresses small opposite-direction updates, directly reducing false      │
