│                          │ local measurement-slope observations support it. This preserves genuine sustained         │
│                          │ reversals with only a short confirmation delay, while preventing isolated noise           │
│                          │ excursions from creating output direction changes. The Kalman state itself remains        │
│                          │ unconstrained, so responsiveness is retained once reversal evidence is established.       │
