│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ robust_velocity_consensus                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed exponentially weighted average with a causal robust local-regression    │
│                          │ tracker. Each window produces an endpoint-aligned trend estimate and local slope using    │
│                          │ two inexpensive Huber reweighting passes. The tracker then combines that local slope with │
│                          │ its prior velocity through a bounded velocity-consensus update.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Unlike a moving average, the local-regression endpoint estimate does not impose the       │
│                          │ approximately half-window lag that drives the current lag error. Unlike a fully reactive  │
│                          │ slope estimate, the bounded consensus limits acceleration according to robust residual    │
│                          │ noise and applies hysteresis only to weak sign reversals. This specifically targets the   │
│                          │ high false-reversal and slope-change counts while retaining prediction-based              │
│                          │ responsiveness during sustained trends. The algorithm remains causal, has output aligned  │
│                          │ to the last sample in each window, and uses only small-window vector operations.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
