│ patch_name               │ multiscale_consensus_tracker                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the low-lag endpoint-regression insight from the stronger prior         │
│                          │ programs, but replaces the expensive per-window Kalman/IRLS pipeline with a multiscale    │
│                          │ robust trend-consensus tracker.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Two robust causal local-linear regressions are computed at different horizons: a short    │
│                          │ horizon detects legitimate acceleration early, while a longer horizon rejects short-lived │
│                          │ noise. Their slope agreement controls the endpoint measurement and adaptive tracker gain. │
│                          │ The sequential tracker then uses a bounded velocity-consensus update: its velocity moves  │
│                          │ toward a blend of the multiscale local slope and the actual filtered step, with           │
│                          │ acceleration limited by local residual noise. A directional confirmation gate suppresses  │
│                          │ weak opposite-direction movements without blocking strong, sustained real reversals. This │
│                          │ directly targets the observed tradeoff between the highly responsive but reversal-heavy   │
│                          │ Kalman variants and the smoother but laggier local-trend variants.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation is vectorized for window feature extraction and has only one           │
│                          │ lightweight streaming loop, substantially reducing latency relative to repeated           │
│                          │ per-window iterative regression.                                                          │
