│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ evidence_gated_reversals                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the existing reversal suppression with explicit, asymmetric evidence gating.   │
│                          │ The present logic updates `stable_velocity` as soon as a candidate velocity crosses a     │
│                          │ noise-scaled threshold, allowing alternating local-regression slopes to create avoidable  │
│                          │ reversals. This edit requires two consecutive, sufficiently strong opposing trend         │
│                          │ indications before a direction change is accepted.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A pending reversal is cancelled when the direct local slope returns to the established    │
│                          │ direction. During the first opposing indication, velocity is gently decayed toward zero   │
│                          │ rather than flipped. This retains the endpoint regression tracker’s low lag on sustained  │
│                          │ turns, while reducing noise-driven slope changes and false reversals—the current primary  │
│                          │ weakness—without adding another filtering pass or material latency.                       │
