│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ evidence_gated_reversal_release                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current reversal counter with direction-aware, volatility-gated evidence. The │
│                          │ existing logic only accumulates evidence when the Kalman velocity has already changed     │
│                          │ sign, which can keep genuine turns frozen because the output hold itself delays the       │
│                          │ velocity update. The revised gate retains one-sample suppression for noise rejection, but │
│                          │ releases a reversal after two consecutive, sufficiently large opposite candidate steps    │
│                          │ even while the Kalman velocity is still transitioning. Large Kalman-supported turns       │
│                          │ continue to bypass confirmation. This should reduce lag and average error while retaining │
│                          │ the current strong reduction in slope changes and false reversals.                        │
