│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hysteretic_trend_controller                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a persistent trend/flat controller around the reported output rather than       │
│                          │ allowing the Kalman level estimate to directly determine every emitted increment. Trend   │
│                          │ entry requires sustained normalized slope evidence, while trend exit uses a lower         │
│                          │ threshold and longer confirmation. This hysteresis prevents gain and direction behavior   │
│                          │ from changing rapidly near the noise floor.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ In flat mode, the output uses a lower tracking gain and stronger velocity damping to      │
│                          │ reduce noise-driven slope changes. In trend mode, it uses a higher gain and faster        │
│                          │ velocity adaptation to retain low lag during genuine movement. Reversal confirmation is   │
│                          │ retained, but uses the controller state and innovation-scaled thresholds so real turns    │
│                          │ can still pass promptly after repeated evidence.                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
