│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multiscale_endpoint_blend                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a small causal multi-scale endpoint-regression ensemble. The existing regression uses │
│                          │ one fixed recency decay, which creates an unavoidable compromise: a gentle profile is     │
│                          │ stable but late during a coherent move, while a steep profile is responsive but can react │
│                          │ to endpoint noise. The edit reuses the robust residual weights from the existing IRLS fit │
│                          │ to compute gentle, current, and steep endpoint fits with only two additional 2x2 solves.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pipeline blends these profiles based on local trend-to-noise ratio and agreement      │
│                          │ between their slopes. In flat or ambiguous windows it retains substantial gentle/current  │
│                          │ influence, reducing spurious directional changes. When all scales independently support   │
│                          │ the same trend, it progressively favors the steep causal endpoint fit, reducing lag       │
│                          │ without relying on a single reactive estimate. The downstream reversal guard remains      │
│                          │ intact as a final protection against unsupported turns.                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
