│ patch_description        │ Replace the single exponential-window reference with a precomputed bank of causal         │
│                          │ endpoint regressions. A gentle decay remains dominant in flat or noisy regions, while     │
│                          │ current and steep recency-weighted fits receive progressively more weight when the fitted │
│                          │ slope is large relative to its residual scale. This supplies a low-lag, trend-aware       │
│                          │ consensus measurement without making the Kalman tracker itself more reactive. The         │
│                          │ existing predictive stage and reversal hysteresis remain in place, preserving their       │
│                          │ false-reversal protection while the improved local reference reduces lag during coherent  │
│                          │ motion.                                                                                   │
