│ patch_description        │ This rewrite replaces the continuously reactive Kalman gain behavior with a robust causal │
│                          │ alpha-beta trend tracker using hysteretic trend-confidence modes.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The enhanced filter estimates local velocity from clipped sample differences and          │
│                          │ maintains separate flat and trend modes. Trend mode is only entered after sustained       │
│                          │ directional evidence and is exited more slowly, preventing gain changes caused by         │
│                          │ individual noisy samples. A counter-trend confirmation mechanism suppresses small         │
│                          │ opposite-direction updates while allowing confirmed genuine reversals through with        │
│                          │ limited delay. Robust innovation clipping and residual-scale adaptation retain protection │
│                          │ against impulsive, non-stationary noise.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The public functions, arguments, output alignment, and return lengths remain compatible   │
