│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ residual_noise_hysteresis                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Separate the robust raw-window scale from the post-fit residual noise estimate. The raw   │
│                          │ MAD is retained only as a small numerical floor for Huber clipping, preventing an almost  │
│                          │ perfectly linear window from producing a near-zero clipping threshold. The residual MAD   │
│                          │ remains the quantity returned to the pipeline and therefore continues to drive trend      │
│                          │ confidence, fusion, strong-turn evidence, and reversal-band sizing. This lets coherent    │
│                          │ ramps retain a low noise estimate rather than being mistaken for volatility.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, weak opposing steps now require three persistent observations before        │
│                          │ reversing, while strong locally and Kalman-supported turns still bypass confirmation.     │
│                          │ This specifically targets the dominant remaining penalties—slope changes and false        │
│                          │ reversals—without imposing the extra delay on decisive genuine turns.                     │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0629                                                                                   │
