│ patch_name               │ adaptive_reversal_hysteresis                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the reporting-layer reversal gate using a wider innovation-normalized          │
│                          │ deadband, three consecutive directionally supported samples, and a higher emergency-turn  │
│                          │ threshold. The current controller treats very small opposite deltas as reversal evidence  │
│                          │ because the qualification threshold is only 20% of an already small band; this admits     │
│                          │ alternating Kalman/consensus jitter. Requiring persistent, velocity-confirmed opposition  │
│                          │ suppresses noise-induced slope changes and false reversals while retaining responsiveness │
│                          │ for genuine turns through the strong-turn escape path. The adaptive band also scales with │
│                          │ emitted velocity, so fast real movements are not reversed by a small counter-trend        │
│                          │ fluctuation.                                                                              │
