│ patch_description        │ Replace sample-by-sample continuous fusion-gain variation with hysteretic discrete flat   │
│                          │ and trend modes. The mode is selected from local slope confidence relative to residual    │
│                          │ noise, requiring two consecutive confident windows to enter responsive trend tracking and │
│                          │ four weak-confidence windows to return to the more conservative flat mode. This prevents  │
│                          │ gain jitter from becoming output-direction jitter, while still allowing a confirmed trend │
│                          │ to use a higher local endpoint-regression gain. The reversal guard is made mode-aware:    │
│                          │ flat/noisy periods require broader evidence before changing direction, whereas confirmed  │
│                          │ trends retain a shorter confirmation path and therefore low lag.                          │
