│ patch_description        │ Replace the three-scale endpoint consensus with two closely related endpoint regressions: │
│                          │ the validated exp(-3) profile and a slightly more recent exp(-4.5) profile. The recent    │
│                          │ profile is not used merely because an instantaneous slope is large; it is admitted only   │
│                          │ after both profiles agree on direction and the trend confidence has persisted across      │
│                          │ consecutive complete windows. This removes conflicting multi-scale slope estimates that   │
│                          │ can produce direction chatter, while preserving the low endpoint lag of local regression  │
│                          │ on clean, sustained trends. The residual-based confidence also makes the blend naturally  │
│                          │ conservative during volatile or noisy intervals.                                          │
