│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ robust_slope_velocity_fusion                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Fuse the accepted consensus motion with a robust short-horizon local slope when updating  │
│                          │ predictive velocity. The current velocity target depends heavily on the Kalman velocity,  │
│                          │ which can remain reactive to innovation noise even when the output reversal gate has held │
│                          │ the consensus level. A median of recent first differences supplies a cheap robust local   │
│                          │ slope estimate that better represents sustained motion.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fusion gives the accepted output step greater weight in flat or noise-dominated       │
│                          │ regions, preventing a noisy slope estimate from restarting motion after a held reversal.  │
│                          │ When the robust local slope is strong and agrees with the Kalman slope, it receives more  │
│                          │ weight, preserving propagation through genuine trends and reducing lag. The existing      │
│                          │ residual-scaled acceleration cap remains in place to prevent abrupt velocity changes.     │
