│                          │ highly reactive, producing excessive slope changes (162.6) and false reversals (128.2).   │
│                          │ This revision retains the causal constant-velocity tracker and low-lag endpoint behavior, │
│                          │ but adds a robust exponentially weighted local-linear slope bank.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - **Robust local regression:** Each sliding window is MAD-clipped before weighted         │
│                          │ fitting, reducing outlier-driven trend reversals.                                         │
│                          │ - **Slope-informed velocity fusion:** The consensus velocity target combines realized     │
│                          │ accepted motion with a robust local slope. In noisy or flat regions, accepted motion has  │
│                          │ greater weight; during confident trends, the fitted local slope contributes more          │
│                          │ strongly.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - **Residual-scaled acceleration cap:** Velocity changes are capped using the local       │
│                          │ residual scale, preventing a single innovation from injecting persistent oscillation.     │
│                          │ - **Stronger reversal hysteresis:** Reversals require two coherent samples unless both    │
│                          │ local slope and candidate displacement provide decisive support.                          │
│                          │ - **Adaptive local-reference blend:** Endpoint regression is used more during coherent    │
│                          │ trends while disagreement with the Kalman state reduces the influence of potentially      │
│                          │ unstable local fits.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Primary parameters are regression recency decay (`3.2`), outlier clipping (`3.5 * MAD`),  │
│                          │ local-reference weight (`0.16` to `0.38`), consensus gain (`0.66` to `0.84`), reversal    │
│                          │ evidence threshold (`2` samples), velocity fusion weighting, and residual-scaled          │
│                          │ acceleration limits.                                                                      │
