│ patch_description        │ Replace continuously varying tracker gains with hysteretic flat and trend modes. The mode │
│                          │ is entered only after two consecutive high-confidence slope windows and exited only after │
│                          │ four low-confidence windows. This prevents local-noise changes in slope confidence from   │
│                          │ directly modulating the gain every sample, which is a likely source of output-direction   │
│                          │ jitter. Flat mode uses conservative level and velocity gains to reduce false reversals,   │
│                          │ while trend mode restores higher gain and anticipatory slope blending for responsive      │
│                          │ tracking of sustained movement.                                                           │
