│ patch_name               │ hysteretic_trend_tracker                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces continuously jittering adaptive gains with hysteretic discrete      │
│                          │ tracking modes. A robust multi-scale, endpoint-aligned regression produces a low-lag      │
│                          │ measurement and trend estimate. The causal tracker remains in a conservative noise/flat   │
│                          │ mode until two consecutive high-confidence trend windows are observed, while it requires  │
│                          │ several low-confidence windows before leaving trend mode.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Confirmed reversals require persistent counter-direction slope evidence, reducing         │
│                          │ noise-induced output direction changes. During confirmed trends, gains are increased      │
│                          │ moderately to retain responsiveness and reduce lag. Innovation gating, robust clipping,   │
│                          │ and velocity deadbands limit outlier influence and false reversals without adding         │
│                          │ non-causal delay.                                                                         │
