│ patch_description        │ Estimate noise after the clipped weighted linear fit using residual MAD, rather than      │
│                          │ using the raw window MAD for trend confidence. Raw window spread grows naturally across   │
│                          │ coherent ramps and oscillations, causing genuine slopes to be classified as uncertain.    │
│                          │ The post-fit residual scale measures only deviations from the local trajectory, so it     │
│                          │ improves responsiveness and trend tracking without weakening the existing window-MAD      │
│                          │ outlier clipping.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also apply the existing reversal band to the countertrend hold condition. The current     │
│                          │ branch suppresses every unconfirmed countertrend step, even when its magnitude is large   │
│                          │ enough to represent a real reversal; `reversal_band` is calculated but unused.            │
│                          │ Restricting suppression to weak countertrend moves retains false-reversal protection      │
│                          │ while releasing substantial turns promptly.                                               │
