╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ robust_pending_turn                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current filter uses an adaptive constant-velocity Kalman tracker, exponentially       │
│                          │ weighted local reference, predictive consensus stage, innovation clipping, and a          │
│                          │ two-sample reversal hysteresis gate. Its main weakness is that relatively weak opposing   │
│                          │ candidate steps can still be released after two samples, contributing to high slope       │
│                          │ changes (162.6) and false reversals (128.2).                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This revision replaces the single EMA local reference with a robust, causally aligned     │
│                          │ endpoint regression. Each sliding window is MAD-clipped before fitting, reducing          │
│                          │ outlier-driven turns while preserving endpoint responsiveness. Key parameter changes are: │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - **Robust regression recency decay:** `2.6`, providing lower endpoint lag than a uniform │
│                          │ moving average without allowing the last sample to dominate.                              │
│                          │ - **Trend confidence:** based on `abs(local_slope) / (abs(local_slope) + 0.65 *           │
│                          │ residual_noise)`, so aggressive local tracking occurs only when slope exceeds residual    │
│                          │ noise.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - **Local-reference fusion weight:** reduced to `0.12–0.38`, preventing regression noise  │
│                          │ from overriding the Kalman state.                                                         │
│                          │ - **Pending reversal state:** every non-decisive countertrend step is suppressed and      │
│                          │ recorded. A reversal is released only on the following coherent sample when candidate     │
│                          │ direction, local slope direction, and residual-noise-scaled step magnitude all agree.     │
│                          │ - **Decisive-turn threshold:** `0.78 * noise_scale`, allowing rapid response to genuine   │
│                          │ sharp extrema without broadly reactive hysteresis.                                        │
│                          │ - **Confirmation threshold:** `0.30 * noise_scale + 0.07 * abs(consensus_velocity)`,      │
│                          │ which reduces false reversals in volatile regions.                                        │
│                          │ - **Acceleration limiting and velocity damping:** limits output curvature and actively    │
│                          │ decelerates a suppressed trend before a confirmed reversal.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting configuration targets substantially fewer noise-induced directional changes │
│                          │ while retaining predictive tracking and causal endpoint alignment.                        │
